WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
Pull a mass on a spring down, and let go.

2
00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:06.530
It bounces, and every
bounce is a little smaller,

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.040
as its trace draws itself.

4
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.680
Which equation produces a
bounce that shrinks like this?

5
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:17.820
In this mission, you'll write acceleration
as the second derivative of displacement.

6
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:21.010
A restoring force pulls
back towards equilibrium,

7
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.840
and a damping force opposes the motion.

8
00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:27.090
You'll turn a second-order
equation into a coupled system,

9
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.210
with y as the velocity.

10
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.020
Then you'll read the motion as a path
in the phase plane that spirals inwards.

11
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:39.160
Your mission: find the equation a spring
obeys when it bounces less each time.
